5. CONTRIBUTIONS AND SUBMISSIONS

AthleteOS may allow users, developers, athletes, coaches, or other
individuals to submit code, suggestions, designs, documentation,
feature requests, bug reports, ideas, or other materials.

Submitting any material does NOT automatically grant permission for that
material to be added to AthleteOS, published, distributed, or incorporated
into the project.

No submitted material may be directly added to the official AthleteOS
codebase, production application, official documentation, or other
official project materials without prior review and approval by an
authorized representative of Nova Code.

Nova Code may review submitted materials and may accept, reject, request
changes to, or decline to use any submission at its sole discretion,
subject to applicable law and any separate written agreement.

A submission is not considered accepted merely because it was received,
reviewed, discussed, or displayed.

Only submissions expressly approved by an authorized representative of
Nova Code may be incorporated into AthleteOS.

Where a separate contribution agreement is provided, that agreement will
govern the ownership and licensing of an accepted contribution.
